    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Scum_and_Villainy\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy\">Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy</a></i> </p><p>If you have the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Quick_Draw\" title=\"Quick Draw\">Quick Draw</a> Feat, you may draw the item as a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Free_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Free Action\">Free Action</a> once per turn. Any <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Equipment\" title=\"Equipment\">Equipment</a> that can be held and used in one hand can be Spring-Loaded. <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Readying\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Readying\">Readying</a> a Spring-Loaded piece of <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Equipment\" title=\"Equipment\">Equipment</a> is a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Swift_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Swift Action\">Swift Action</a>. It is most common for <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pistols\" title=\"Pistols\">Pistols</a> to be Spring-Loaded, but anything from <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Grenades\" title=\"Grenades\">Grenades</a> to <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Datapad\" title=\"Datapad\">Datapads</a> can use this Upgrade. </p>",
